  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.346,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.829,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the length of the side of a square with an area of 49 sq. cm is 7 cm. We call 7 the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "square root",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of 49."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.125,
            0.622,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { i f }   y   \\stackrel { - } { = }   x ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then x is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "square root",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of y."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.154,
            0.448,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What is the square root of 64?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.179,
            0.848,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "8 \\times 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is 64. So, 8 is the square root of 64. What about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- 8 \\times - 8 ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " That is 64 too!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.215,
            0.607,
            0.234
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "8^{2}=64,\\mathrm{and}(-8)^{2}=64."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.234,
            0.549,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the square roots of 64 are + 8 and – 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.253,
            0.846,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Every perfect square has two integer square roots. One is positive and the other is negative. The square root of a number is denoted by Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 6 4 } }   =   \\pm 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 1 0 0 }   =   \\pm 1 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.316,
            0.765,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 8 ^ { 2 } } }   =   \\pm 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 1 0 ^ { 2 } }   =   \\pm 1 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . In general, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { n ^ { 2 } } }   =   \\pm n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In this chapter, we shall only consider the positive square root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.368,
            0.801,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Given a number, such as 576 or 327, how do we find out if it is a perfect square? If it is a perfect square, how can we find its square root?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.373,
            0.904,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.817,
                0.373,
                0.904,
                0.43
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.43,
            0.847,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that perfect squares end in 1, 4, 9, 6, 5, or an even number of zeros. But, it is not certain that a number that satisfies this condition is a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.485,
            0.847,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can clearly say that 327 is not a perfect square. However, we cannot be sure that 576 is a perfect square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.527,
            0.848,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. We can list all the square numbers in sequence and find out whether 576 occurs among them. We know that 202 = 400, we can find squares of 21, 22, 23, … and so on until we get 576 or a number greater than 576."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.611,
            0.294,
            0.631
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "2 0 ^ { 2 } = 4 0 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.612,
            0.417,
            0.631
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "2 1 ^ { 2 } = 4 4 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.453,
            0.611,
            0.546,
            0.631
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "22^{2} = 484"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.579,
            0.611,
            0.67,
            0.631
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "2 3 ^ { 2 } = 5 2 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.705,
            0.611,
            0.796,
            0.631
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "2 4 ^ { 2 } = 5 7 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.642,
            0.792,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "However, this process becomes inefficient for larger numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.672,
            0.847,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Recall that every square can be expressed as a sum of consecutive odd numbers starting from 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.716,
            0.325,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 8 1 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.757,
            0.296,
            0.775
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_22.jpg",
          "content": "81 - 1 = 80"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.757,
            0.416,
            0.775
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_23.jpg",
          "content": "80 - 3 = 77"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.559,
            0.757,
            0.664,
            0.775
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_24.jpg",
          "content": "72 - 7 = 65"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.757,
            0.794,
            0.775
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_25.jpg",
          "content": "65 - 9 = 56"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.786,
            0.306,
            0.806
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_26.jpg",
          "content": "56 - 11 = 45"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.787,
            0.447,
            0.806
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_27.jpg",
          "content": "45 - 13 = 32"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.478,
            0.786,
            0.594,
            0.806
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_28.jpg",
          "content": "32 - 15 = 17"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.628,
            0.787,
            0.733,
            0.806
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_29.jpg",
          "content": "1 7 - 1 7 = 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.827,
            0.847,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From 81, we successively subtracted consecutive odd numbers starting from 1 until we obtained 0 at the 9th step. Therefore "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 8 1 } }   = 9"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.873,
            0.848,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we find the square root of 729 using this method? Yes, but it will be time-consuming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.915,
            0.112,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
